      "headline": "Pacific Amphitheatre: 16 Shows Over 5 Decades",
      "prose": "I've been returning to Pacific Amphitheatre in Costa Mesa for nearly 40 years now, starting with Tears For Fears in 1985 when I was young enough to think outdoor concerts in July were a good idea. Sixteen shows across five decades means this venue has been a constant through every phase of my life — from that first synth-pop experience to catching The English Beat just this past summer. Something about the way sound carries in that amphitheater keeps pulling me back, whether it's for multiple Beach Boys shows or discovering acts like The Art of Noise live. I realize now that Pacific Amphitheatre isn't just where I see concerts — it's where I measure time.",
