      "temporality": "evergreen",
      "headline": "Crowded House: From Opener to Headliner",
      "prose": "Crowded House's trajectory from Melbourne alt-rock darlings to enduring pop craftsmen spans exactly the 30 years between when I saw them open for Peter Gabriel at the Olympic Velodrome in 1993 and headline The Wiltern in 2023. That first show came around the time *Woodface* had established them as more than just Neil Finn's post-Split Enz project, but they were still very much the supporting act in a massive arena. Three decades later, watching them command their own stage at the Wiltern felt like witnessing the full arc of a band that never chased trends but simply outlasted them. Some artists earn their headliner status through persistence and craft rather than flash.",
