      "headline": "Depeche Mode: 38 Years of Shows",
      "prose": "I still remember walking into Irvine Meadows in 1985 for my first Depeche Mode show, when they were just five years into their career and still riding the wave of their early synthpop sound. That night kicked off what became a 38-year relationship with their live performances, spanning four decades and taking me from Southern California amphitheaters to the gleaming Kia Forum just last year. Five shows across nearly four decades feels almost modest for a band this essential to my concert-going life, but each one marked a different era of both their evolution and mine. There's something beautifully cyclical about starting and ending this run in the same corner of Los Angeles County.",
