      "headline": "Squeeze: From Opener to Headliner",
      "prose": "Few bands embodied the scrappy spirit of new wave quite like Squeeze, and my concert history accidentally documented their long climb from opening act to headliner. I first saw them opening for Oingo Boingo at a racetrack in Tijuana in 1987, when their clever wordplay and pub rock energy felt perfectly suited to warming up a crowd. Twenty-five years later, I watched them headline Rams Head Live in Baltimore, now seasoned veterans commanding the stage with the same wit but deeper confidence. It's rare to witness that complete arc in your own concert diary — from promising opener to rightful headliner.",
